window.docContents[39].resolve({"/Appendix/#chapter-appendix":{"contents":"namespace SimpleGraph\nvariable {V : Type*} {G : SimpleGraph V}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean","header":"15. Appendix","id":"/Appendix/#chapter-appendix"},"/Appendix/#section-chapter-13-theorems-results":{"contents":"* exists_isMatching_of_forall_ncard_le': Hall's theorem for one side of a\nbipartite graph, without assuming local finiteness.* exists_isMatching_of_forall_ncard_le_add: Hall's theorem with deficiency d — if\nevery s ⊆ p₁ has at least |s| - d neighbours, a matching covers all but at most\nd vertices of p₁.* IsBipartite.matchingNum_eq_vertexCoverNum: Kőnig's theorem — ν G = τ G for a\nfinite bipartite graph.* vertexCoverNum_hypercube_succ: τ Q[n + 1] = 2 ^ n, by Kőnig's theorem.* IsCompleteMultipartite.nonempty_iso_turanGraph: a complete multipartite\n(r + 1)-clique-free graph with balanced parts, to which no edge can be added\nwithout creating an (r + 1)-clique, is isomorphic to the Turán graph.* CliqueFree.exists_colorable_two_mul_card_edgeFinset_le: Füredi's stability\ntheorem — an (r + 1)-clique-free graph can be made r-colourable by deleting at\nmost turanNumber n r - e(G) edges.* card_cliqueFinset_replaceVertex: giving b the neighbours of a (the graph\nG.replaceVertex a b) removes the s-cliques through b and adds as many as\nthere are s-cliques through a but not b.* IsCompleteMultipartite.exists_isNClique_of_le: in a complete multipartite graph\nwith an s-clique (2 ≤ s), any edge x — y of a larger graph lies in an\ns-clique of that graph.* IsNCliqueMaximal.nonempty_iso_turanGraph: an (r + 1)-clique-free graph with\nthe most s-cliques, where 2 ≤ s, is a Turán graph if it has an s-clique at\nall.* Iso.card_cliqueFinset_eq: isomorphic graphs have the same number of s-cliques.* CliqueFree.card_cliqueFinset_le: Zykov's theorem — an (r + 1)-clique-free graph\non n vertices has at most as many s-cliques as T[n, r].* CliqueFree.card_cliqueFinset_eq_iff_nonempty_iso_turanGraph: uniqueness in\nZykov's theorem — for 2 ≤ s ≤ r and s ≤ n, an (r + 1)-clique-free graph has\nas many s-cliques as T[n, r] iff it is isomorphic to it.* EdgeDisjointTriangles.card_cliqueFinset_lt: a graph on n vertices whose\ntriangles are edge-disjoint has less than ε * n² triangles once n is large.* ruzsaSzemerediNumberNat_isLittleO: the Ruzsa–Szemerédi number of n is\no(n²).* mem_end_iff: the ends of G, as defined in Mathlib, are exactly its directions.* ComponentCompl.mem_of_hom: the image of a connected graph under a homomorphism\navoiding K lies in a single component of G - K.\n\nMathlib theorems surveyed in this chapter:\n\n* exists_isMatching_of_forall_ncard_le /\nexists_isPerfectMatching_of_forall_ncard_le: Hall's marriage theorem for locally\nfinite bipartite graphs, giving a matching that covers one side, or a perfect\nmatching.* Subgraph.IsPerfectMatching.symmDiff_isCycles: the symmetric difference of two\nperfect matchings is a disjoint union of cycles.* tutte: Tutte's theorem — a finite graph has a perfect matching iff it has no\nTutte violator.* isTuranMaximal_iff_nonempty_iso_turanGraph: Turán's theorem — for 0 < r the\nK[r + 1]-free graphs with the most edges are exactly the Turán graphs.* CliqueFree.card_edgeFinset_le: a K[r + 1]-free graph on n vertices has at\nmost turanNumber n r edges; with turanNumber_two this is Mantel's theorem.* IsBipartite.four_mul_encard_edgeSet_le: a bipartite graph on n vertices has\nat most n ^ 2 / 4 edges, with ℕ∞-valued cardinalities so that no finiteness\nassumption is needed.* colorable_of_cliqueFree_lt_minDegree: the Andrásfai–Erdős–Sós theorem — a\nK[r + 1]-free graph of large minimum degree is r-colourable.* extremalNumber_top: Turán's theorem for extremal numbers — the extremal number\nof a complete graph on r + 1 vertices is the number of edges of T[n, r].* tendsto_turanDensity / isEquivalent_extremalNumber: the extremal number of H\nis asymptotically its Turán density times n.choose 2.* eventually_completeEquipartiteGraph_isContained_of_minDegree: the Erdős–Stone\ntheorem, in its minimum degree form.* szemeredi_regularity: Szemerédi's regularity lemma.* triangle_removal: the triangle removal lemma.* roth_3ap_theorem_nat: Roth's theorem — a set of natural numbers of positive\ndensity contains a three-term arithmetic progression.* corners_theorem_nat: the corners theorem — a dense set of points in the grid\ncontains a corner (x, y), (x + d, y), (x, y + d) with d ≠ 0.* exists_seq_covby_of_forall_covby_finite: Kőnig's lemma, in an order-theoretic\nform.* nonempty_ends_of_infinite: an infinite, connected, locally finite graph has at\nleast one end.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* IsRegularOfDegree.exists_isPerfectMatching: a k-regular bipartite graph with\nk > 0, not necessarily finite, has a perfect matching.* IsRegularOfDegree.colorable_lineGraph: Kőnig's line colouring theorem for regular\ngraphs — the edges of a k-regular bipartite graph can be properly coloured with\nk colours.* card_cliqueFinset_two: a graph has as many 2-cliques as edges, so Zykov's\ntheorem for s = 2 is the edge bound of Turán's theorem.* sum_degree_le_erdosGallai: the degrees of a set S of k vertices sum to at\nmost k * (k - 1) + ∑ v ∈ Sᶜ, min k (G.degree v).* Graphic.erdosGallaiLE: a graphic multiset satisfies the Erdős–Gallai\ninequalities, so with Graphic.even_sum the conditions in erdos_gallai are\nnecessary.\n\nend SimpleGraph\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Results","header":"Chapter 13: Theorems (Results)","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-13-theorems-results"}});